{"availability":"available","full":"usr-wwelsh/omniMux","name":"omniMux","description":"Self-hosted music server with a Spotify-style PWA — search YouTube, save tracks to your own library, and stream from anywhere. AutoDJ crossfades, visualizers, multi-device sync. Navidrome + FastAPI + SvelteKit.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Svelte","stars":2,"forks":0,"created":"2026-04-01T14:59:41Z","updated":"2026-10-10T17:32:58Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://omnimux.wwel.sh","topics":["degoogle","docker","fastapi","homelab","music","music-player","music-server","music-streaming","navidrome","offline-first","pwa","self-hosted","selfhosted","spotify-alternative","subsonic","sveltekit","youtube","youtube-music","yt-dlp","ytmusicapi"],"demo":"https://omnimux.wwel.sh/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T14:52:57.487Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T14:52:57.487Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T14:52:57.487Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T14:52:57.487Z","stars":2,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Svelte","Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A self-hosted music server that lets you search YouTube, cache tracks to your library, and stream everything through a Spotify-like PWA. Built on top of Navidrome with a FastAPI middleware layer and a SvelteKit frontend.","Live demo → omnimux.wwel.sh (guest access, read-only library)","Streaming services rent you access to music you'll never own, lock your library behind monthly fees, and vanish the moment licensing deals fall through. omniMux flips that: search YouTube, keep the files on your own hardware, and stream them from anywhere over a PWA you install once. No cloud. No subscription. No gatekeepers. Just your music, on your server."],"features":["Beat-locked crossfades, tempo matching, and realistic pitch/speed slop — plus 10+ music visualizers driven by high-res iTunes album art.","Find any track and cache it locally. Topic channel results rank first for clea